WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.396 --> 00:00:19.500
While Little John pretended to be a friar, Robin Hood was going to pretend to be a beggar.

2
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.582
But Robin still needed a beggar's clothes.

3
00:00:23.402 --> 00:00:28.406
He walked all morning, enjoying the warm sunshine and fresh smells of springtime.

4
00:00:29.346 --> 00:00:31.428
But he didn't meet any beggars.

5
00:00:32.312 --> 00:00:34.853
"I'm getting hungry," Robin said to himself.

6
00:00:35.473 --> 00:00:43.437
He began imagining a delicious meal with eggs, freshly baked bread, a meat pie Just then Robin rounded

7
00:00:43.497 --> 00:00:46.118
a corner and spotted a beggar sitting on a wall.

8
00:00:46.938 --> 00:00:50.200
The man wore a leather cap on top of his curly dark hair.

9
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.381
He was surrounded by all kinds of pouches and bags.

10
00:00:54.401 --> 00:00:56.382
"Hello, fine fellow!"

11
00:00:56.742 --> 00:00:57.363
said Robin.

12
00:00:57.383 --> 00:00:59.944
"Do you know where I can find something to eat?"

13
00:01:01.164 --> 00:01:02.805
The beggar had friendly eyes.

14
00:01:02.825 --> 00:01:08.049
"I usually eat just a crust of bread and some water," he said.

15
00:01:08.069 --> 00:01:09.610
Robin laughed.

16
00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:13.072
"I can't believe that's all you have in those bags."

17
00:01:13.092 --> 00:01:18.216
"Well, I might have a little cheese," the beggar said slyly.

18
00:01:18.236 --> 00:01:20.537
"Or maybe even some meat.

19
00:01:21.238 --> 00:01:25.541
There's an inn nearby, but they've banned me for stealing a pie.

20
00:01:26.261 --> 00:01:29.684
If you go and buy us drinks, I'll share my food with you."

21
00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.081
"Agreed!" said Robin eagerly.

22
00:01:34.361 --> 00:01:37.642
When Robin returned, the two men began eating lunch.

23
00:01:37.662 --> 00:01:40.903
"I'd like to try being a beggar," said Robin.

24
00:01:40.923 --> 00:01:42.823
"Will you sell me your clothes?"

25
00:01:43.444 --> 00:01:46.104
The beggar narrowed his eyes with suspicion.

26
00:01:46.124 --> 00:01:50.806
"You need more than the right clothes to be a good beggar!

27
00:01:51.466 --> 00:01:55.447
It takes a long time to learn how to beg properly.

28
00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.908
But let's have a fighting match with our staffs.

29
00:01:59.648 --> 00:02:02.671
If you defeat me, I'll sell you my clothes."

30
00:02:03.773 --> 00:02:07.156
So the two men finished their lunch and picked up their staffs.

31
00:02:09.818 --> 00:02:13.402
In a few minutes the beggar was lying on the ground, rubbing his head.

32
00:02:14.003 --> 00:02:17.866
Robin counted out some coins, and the two men exchanged clothes.

33
00:02:17.886 --> 00:02:20.969
"Thank you, my friend," said Robin.

34
00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:23.372
"Now I'm ready for adventure."

35
00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.141
Robin began walking along the road, which led up a gentle hill.

36
00:02:30.462 --> 00:02:35.183
He had walked for a long time when he came across four more beggars, resting in a meadow.

37
00:02:35.803 --> 00:02:37.924
Each man wore a sign around his neck.

38
00:02:38.644 --> 00:02:42.645
As Robin approached, one beggar said, "I hear someone coming!"

39
00:02:43.225 --> 00:02:45.346
His sign said, "I'm Deaf."

40
00:02:46.446 --> 00:02:49.207
"He looks like another beggar," said the second man.

41
00:02:49.807 --> 00:02:52.268
His sign said, "I'm Blind."

42
00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.861
The third man called out to Robin.

43
00:02:54.881 --> 00:02:56.681
"Welcome, fellow beggar!"

44
00:02:57.361 --> 00:02:59.642
His sign said, "I Can't Talk."

45
00:02:59.662 --> 00:03:02.003
"Come sit with us!"

46
00:03:02.463 --> 00:03:03.303
said the fourth man.

47
00:03:03.843 --> 00:03:05.984
He stood up and made room for Robin.

48
00:03:06.624 --> 00:03:08.544
His sign said, "I'm Lame."

49
00:03:08.564 --> 00:03:11.685
"Thank you, I will."

50
00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:13.286
Robin laughed.

51
00:03:13.306 --> 00:03:16.146
"What a merry group of cheaters!"

52
00:03:16.166 --> 00:03:17.947
"Where did you come from?"

53
00:03:18.287 --> 00:03:19.327
asked the blind beggar.

54
00:03:19.347 --> 00:03:23.297
"I spent last night in Sherwood Forest," said Robin.

55
00:03:23.317 --> 00:03:25.959
"You couldn't pay me to sleep there!"

56
00:03:26.219 --> 00:03:27.540
exclaimed the deaf beggar.

57
00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.804
"If Robin Hood knew we were tricking people into giving us money, he'd come after us."

58
00:03:32.824 --> 00:03:36.127
"That's right," agreed the lame beggar.

59
00:03:36.147 --> 00:03:39.290
"I wouldn't sleep in Sherwood Forest either.

60
00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:43.113
Not with all the money we're carrying right now for the king.

61
00:03:43.873 --> 00:03:46.476
Why, we have—" "Shh!"

62
00:03:47.076 --> 00:03:49.358
The blind beggar silenced the lame man.

63
00:03:49.378 --> 00:03:51.580
"What money are you talking about?"

64
00:03:52.052 --> 00:03:53.472
Robin asked pleasantly.

65
00:03:57.414 --> 00:04:00.134
The men grabbed their staffs and leaped to their feet.

66
00:04:00.835 --> 00:04:02.015
They stepped toward Robin.

67
00:04:02.655 --> 00:04:03.795
Robin jumped up too.

68
00:04:03.815 --> 00:04:06.876
"The four of you are going to attack me?"

69
00:04:07.236 --> 00:04:07.697
he said.

70
00:04:08.717 --> 00:04:10.297
He twirled his own staff.

71
00:04:10.317 --> 00:04:13.258
"Why? I haven't done you any harm."

72
00:04:13.978 --> 00:04:15.699
"Liar! You're a spy!"

73
00:04:16.119 --> 00:04:17.079
cried the blind man.

74
00:04:17.099 --> 00:04:19.340
"You've heard too much."

75
00:04:21.404 --> 00:04:24.445
He attacked Robin, who quickly knocked him to the ground.

76
00:04:25.126 --> 00:04:28.467
The man rolled over and over on the grass and didn't move.

77
00:04:28.487 --> 00:04:30.408
"Who's next?"

78
00:04:31.248 --> 00:04:34.590
Robin rushed at the three men and struck the deaf man.

79
00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.051
The deaf man fell to the ground.

80
00:04:37.651 --> 00:04:42.813
The other two beggars looked at Robin with terror, and ran away as fast as they could.

81
00:04:44.294 --> 00:04:45.914
Robin stood there, laughing.

82
00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:50.076
"I've never seen anyone run as fast as that lame man!

83
00:04:50.672 --> 00:04:52.794
Now let's see where that money is."

84
00:04:53.574 --> 00:04:56.156
Robin searched through the beggars' pockets and pouches.

85
00:04:56.857 --> 00:05:00.319
He soon found two hundred pounds in gold coins.

86
00:05:00.339 --> 00:05:04.883
"Those beggars got this money by tricking people," Robin said.

87
00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:07.224
"I'll take it and give it to charity."

88
00:05:08.765 --> 00:05:12.508
Robin started walking along the road, singing and whistling as he went.

89
00:05:14.089 --> 00:05:17.572
Every pretty girl he met smiled and greeted him sweetly.

90
00:05:18.528 --> 00:05:23.875
And every dog he met wagged its tail, and sniffed at his legs, happy to see him.

91
00:05:23.895 --> 00:05:28.361
"Dogs usually mistrust beggars," Robin thought.

92
00:05:28.381 --> 00:05:31.885
"But they always know an honest man by his smell."

93
00:05:32.706 --> 00:05:35.710
Robin was an honest man—in his own way.
